Description: TemporalModelR is an R package built with the goal of increasing
    the ease of implementing a temporally-explicit modeling methodology when
    building ecological niche and species distribution models. It provides
    functions to assist with three major steps of temporally-explicit
    models: (i) preprocessing species and environmental data and generating
    suitable background or pseudoabsence data, (ii) building a niche model
    and generating temporally-explicit predictions from that model, and
    (iii) model postprocessing to explore spatiotemporal trends in model
    predictions.
